Workspace Configuration

1. tsconfig.json —
   json
   {
   "compilerOptions": {
   "target": "ES2021",
   "module": "commonjs",
   "strict": true,
   "esModuleInterop": true,
   "skipLibCheck": true
   }
   }
   strict: true — this is why TypeScript has been catching all your type errors since Day 1. Never turn this off.
   target: which JavaScript version your code compiles down to. ES2021+ supports modern features you've used (optional chaining, nullish coalescing).
   esModuleInterop: makes import/export (Day 10 style) work smoothly with older-style JavaScript modules.

2. Multi-root workspaces (optional but useful concept)

If you ever want your Day 1-20 practice folder (ts_practice) and your Day 13+ Playwright project (playwright-framework) open side by side in one VS Code window:

File → Add Folder to Workspace → select the second folder
File → Save Workspace As → saves a .code-workspace file

3. .vscode/settings.json — project-specific overrides (expanding Day 21)

Beyond formatting, you can scope settings to just this project:

json
{
"editor.formatOnSave": true,
"typescript.updateImportsOnFileMove.enabled": "always",
"files.exclude": {
"**/node_modules": true,
"**/test-results": true,
"\*\*/playwright-report": true
}
}

files.exclude hides clutter folders from your VS Code file explorer sidebar — you'll thank yourself once node_modules has thousands of files you never need to see.
